.page trap 1 run a command when the shell exits

# SYNOPSIS
*trap* _COMMAND_ *EXIT*
*trap* '' _SIGNAL_...

# DESCRIPTION
`trap` is a gapsh builtin. `trap 'COMMANDS' EXIT` (or `0`) arranges for _COMMANDS_ to be run when the shell exits; `trap - EXIT` removes it. For signals only two things are supported: `trap '' SIGNAL` ignores the signal, and any other command restores its default action. The signal can be given as a number or a name with or without `SIG`.

# EXAMPLES
    trap 'rm -f /tmp/work.$$' EXIT
    trap '' INT

# SEE ALSO
exit(1), kill(1)
